# Version

## Current Version

`0.7.7`

## Version Type

Minor model-feature release over `0.7.6`.

This version implements Phase 4 reopening of clarification after Human2 rejects insufficient detail at the `@office-dsl/intent-contract-model` diagnosis layer. `ApprovalNode` can now carry optional rejected-field context (`field`, `reason`, and `source`), and `diagnoseIntentContractDsl` reports rejected approvals, blocks finalization, and generates a reopened clarification question routed to Human1 when Human2 rejects a field.

The Phase 3 diagnosis, Phase 4 question routing, conversation input format, mock conversation-history planner, and rejected-approval reopening are model/planner layers only. Live runtime, CLI, backend, and UI integration of rejection-driven clarification remains open (Phases 11 and 12). No OCR or document-ingestion behavior is implemented in this version; Phase 4B is roadmap documentation only.

